 {
  "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/aim/PAF-AVS-V1.6",
  "@type": [
   "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#AIM"
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#acronym": [
   {
    "@value": "PAF-AVS-V1.6"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#apiProfile": [
   {
    "@value": "Secure"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "Avatar Videoconference Server (slide 3 of the PAF Reference Models): it has two Portable Avatar inputs, both the Portable Avatars of the Virtual Meeting Secretary and of the participants - the first (Port 1) is the set of all the Portable Avatars received and goes straight to Portable Avatar Multiplexing, unchanged and not acted upon, the second (Port 2) is the subset that goes to Portable Avatar Demultiplexing and through translation - all of them unless no participant speaks the same language as another. The Portable Avatars of the participants have no room and no seat: the Multimodal Scene Descriptors and the Spatial Attitudes the server adds are those of its own room. At the start, it receives the Portable Avatars and the Speech and Face Objects of the participants, authenticates them, and distributes the Portable Avatars with the Audio-Visual Scene, the Spatial Attitudes and the Avatar IDs; during the meeting it translates the text and speech of the participants and of the Virtual Meeting Secretary according to their language preferences, and distributes the Portable Avatars. The Summary of the Virtual Meeting Secretary passes through. It is the Trust Authority of the participants and of the Virtual Meeting Secretary; its External Ports (IsRemote) take from and give to their Controllers through Communication, a Portable Avatar going to every one but the one it came from; the Audio-Visual Scene and the Spatial Attitudes are its own. It runs continuously."
   }
  ],
