 {
  "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/aim/MMC-VCI-V2.5",
  "@type": [
   "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#AIM"
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#acronym": [
   {
    "@value": "MMC-VCI-V2.5"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#apiProfile": [
   {
    "@value": "Basic"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "Voice Command Interface: a person talks to an application and the application answers aloud. The same for every application: the application is given to it as the schemas of its commands and of its responses and the rest of the Application Context (MMC-APC), which JSON Interface (MMC-JSI) takes from the AccessSources of its L3 or receives on the Application Context Port. Automatic Speech Recognition recognises the speech; JSON Interface turns what the person asked into the command that conforms to the application's schema - for Audio Scene Management, a User Command (CAE-UCM) request - and turns the application's response, a User Command response, into the Response Hint; Entity Dialogue Processing, which holds the dialogue, says what is to be said - an answer, a question when the request is not clear, what was done or why not - from the recognised text and the Response Hint; Text to Speech speaks it. The command goes out on a Port and the response comes in on a Port, whatever the application. The speech that carries commands is not the speech an application edits: they arrive on different Ports. A response is said when it arrives: the application may take time."
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#flow": [
   {
    "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/aim/MMC-VCI-V2.5/flow/1"
   },
   {
