 {
  "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/aim/PGM-AUF-V1.0",
  "@type": [
   "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#AIM"
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#acronym": [
   {
    "@value": "PGM-AUF-V1.0"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#apiProfile": [
   {
    "@value": "Basic"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#code": [
   {
    "@id": "https://github.com/leonardo-chiariglione/mpai-sw/blob/main/AIMs/PGM/V1.0/AufAims.cs"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#codePath": [
   {
    "@value": "AIMs/PGM/V1.0/AufAims.cs"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "The A-User Formation (PGM-AUF) AIM forms the Portable Avatar that utters the A-User's response. It combines the deliberated communicative content (the Final Response produced by Basic Knowledge: the text, the Actions and the Process Actions) with the A-User State produced by Personality Alignment. The Portable Avatar expresses the A-User's Personal Status across speech, face, and body. A-User Formation is driven by the AUC-AUF Request of A-User Control. Its function is that of Response and Scene Rendering (PAF-RSR) of MPAI-PAF, to which it adds the Request and the Response of the A-User Control AIM and the taking apart of the Final Response: the Process Actions are given to A-User Control unchanged, the Communicative Functions are given a Behaviour and times on the Machine Speech by Behaviour Planning, and they and the Actions become the Animation Objects of the face and the body. The response reports, for each Communicative Function, whether it was realised."
   }
  ],
