   {
    "@value": "AIMs/CAE3/V1.0/ASE/AseAimProcessor.cs"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "Audio Scene Editing. One Audio Scene is open at a time, so a User Command need not name it: a Audio Scene arriving is opened, and the first Object added to no open Scene creates one. The User Command places Audio Objects - named as the User names them - (AddedObjects), moves them (MovedObjects), changes where they are (ChangedObjects), takes them out (RemovedObjects) and sets where the Scene is heard from (UserPoV). Every edit is a new version in Shared Storage. Outputs: the open Audio Scene, and the User Command, with its response (UserCommandRS) saying how each action was executed."
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#ofStandard": [
   {
    "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/standard/CAE"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#port": [
