 {
  "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/datatype/TFA-SAQ-V1.5",
  "@type": [
   "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#DataType"
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#acronym": [
   {
    "@value": "TFA-SAQ-V1.5"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "Qualifier stating the conventions by which the numbers of a Spatial Attitude, of Spatial Data and of Pointing Data are to be read: the representation, the reference frame, the axes and their handedness, the units and the order of the rotations. It states what the data cannot state, and it does not change them. When the Qualifier is absent, the default conventions of the Data Type apply. For Position, Orientation and Spatial Attitude (OSD) they are those of ISO 8855: a right-handed East-North-Up frame; body axes X forward, Y left, Z up; Euler angles (α, β, γ) = (yaw, pitch, roll), intrinsic rotations about Z, Y′, X″, positive by the right-hand rule; degrees and metres; a quaternion (w, x, y, z). A Data Type with no stated default does not state its conventions. A Qualifier carried by a Data Type that contains another (a Path of Points of View, a Spatial Attitude with its Position and Orientation) applies to what it contains, unless the contained Data Type carries its own."
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#ofStandard": [
   {
    "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/standard/TFA"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#schema": [
   {
    "@id": "https://schemas.mpai.community/TFA/V1.5/data/SpatialQualifier.json"
   }
  ],
