 {
  "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/aim/OSD-BME-V1.5",
  "@type": [
   "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#AIM"
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#acronym": [
   {
    "@value": "OSD-BME-V1.5"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#apiProfile": [
   {
    "@value": "Basic"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "Basic Multimodal Scene Editing: Basic Scenes and Basic Objects of at least two media - Audio, Visual, Speech, LiDAR, 3D Model, RADAR, Ultrasound, Offline Map - composed into a Basic Multimodal Scene (a voice over music is a BMS of a BAS and a BSS, or of a BAO and a BSO). It is Multimodal Scene Editing (OSD-MSE) working on the Basic Scenes and Basic Objects: each of its two Scene Ports takes a Basic Scene of any medium, each of its two Object Ports a Basic Object of any medium, and the User Command (with the User PoV, optional) places, moves, changes and removes them in the one open Basic Multimodal Scene; the User Command with its response leaves on the second output."
   }
  ],
