  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "Speech Scene Editing. One Speech Scene is open at a time: a Speech Scene arriving is opened, and the first Object added to no open Scene creates one. The User Command places Speech Objects - named as the User names them - (AddedObjects), moves them, changes where they are, takes them out and sets where the Scene is heard from (UserPoV). Every edit is a new version in Shared Storage; a member is held by its identifier and read from Shared Storage when the Scene is output. Outputs: the open Speech Scene, and the User Command, with its response (UserCommandRS) saying how each action was executed."
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#ofStandard": [
   {
    "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/standard/MMC"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#port": [
