 {
  "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/datatype/AIF-LIC-V3.0",
  "@type": [
   "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#DataType"
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#acronym": [
   {
    "@value": "AIF-LIC-V3.0"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#code": [
   {
    "@id": "https://github.com/leonardo-chiariglione/mpai-sw/blob/main/Store/AimLicences.cs"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#codePath": [
   {
    "@value": "Store/AimLicences.cs"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#description": [
   {
    "@value": "The licence of an AIM, in two states of one Data Type. As an OFFER - the AIMLicence field of AIM Metadata, which the Implementer fills and the MPAI Store publishes once, for everybody - it states Grant, the Term it grants for, Updates, the price (Payment, a Service Pricing Model) and where its terms are (TermsURI); it has no Licensee and no Signature. As an ISSUED AIM Licence - what the MPAI Store gives a Controller that obtains the AIM - it is the offer completed for that licensee: AIMLicenceID, AIMLicenceTime, AIM (the files covered, with the fingerprints the MPAI Store approved), Licensor (the MPAI Store), Licensee, a Term with its NotBefore, Status (where revocation is asked), Payment as a Final Service Pricing Model with its Settlement (proof of acquisition), and the Signature of the MPAI Store. A Controller keeps the issued AIM Licence with the AIM in its AIM repository and checks it before it builds the AIM: the signature is the MPAI Store's, it names this Controller, its fingerprints are those of what is built, its Term has not ended, its Grant covers the use and, when the MPAI Store can be reached, it is not revoked. An AIM whose Metadata has no AIMLicence needs no AIM Licence. THE TWO LICENCES: the offer is the Implementer's licence to the MPAI Store, which states what the MPAI Store may grant (Grant, Term, Updates, the Implementer's proposed price in Payment) and, in Sublicensing, that it may sublicense; the issued AIM Licence is the MPAI Store's sublicence to the Entity that runs Controllers (the holder of a PTF Trust Anchor: an organisation, one owner, the operator of a MAS service), within the offer, at the price proposed by the Implementer with the MPAI Store's mark-up applied, and names the offer it is under in ParentLicence."
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#ofStandard": [
   {
    "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/standard/AIF"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#schema": [
   {
    "@id": "https://schemas.mpai.community/AIF/V3.0/data/AIMLicence.json"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#sourceAI": [
   {
    "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean",
    "@value": true
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#title": [
   {
    "@value": "AIM Licence V3.0"
   }
  ],
  "https://mpai.community/kg/vocab#uses": [
   {
    "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/datatype/PTF/SecurityAlgorithmTaxonomy"
   },
   {
    "@id": "https://mpai.community/kg/datatype/PTF-DEM-V1.0"
   },
